---
// /notices/: the public notices of moderation (night phase 16; docs/MODERATION.md, docs/POLICIES.md):
// what kind of thing was hidden or restored, why, when, and the owner's redacted words — never the
// hidden words themselves, never who reported. As of last night (src/lib/moderated.ts). One page,
// static. science.css only.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../config";
import { NOTICES } from "../lib/moderated";
---
<Base
  title="Moderation notices"
  description="What was hidden from the registry's pages, why and when, and what was restored: redacted public notices."
  breadcrumb={[{ text: "Acceptable use", href: "/acceptable-use/" }, { text: "Moderation notices" }]}
>
  <h1>Moderation notices</h1>
  <p class="summary">
    {NOTICES.length ? `${NOTICES.length.toLocaleString("en-GB")} ${NOTICES.length === 1 ? "decision" : "decisions"}, the newest first, as of last night.` : "No decision yet."}
  </p>
  <p>
    When {SITE_NAME}'s owner hides something from the registry's pages — after a report, a takedown notice or
    the registry's own check for known malware — a notice is published here: what kind of thing, why, when, and
    whether it was restored. A notice never repeats the hidden words, never names who reported it, and never
    publishes private information. The rules are the <a href="/acceptable-use/">acceptable-use policy</a> and the{" "}
    <a href="/terms/">terms</a>; takedowns and counter-notices are explained on <a href="/copyright/">the
    takedown page</a>.
  </p>
  {NOTICES.length > 0 && (
    <table class="queue">
      <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>What</th><th>Why</th><th>Notice</th><th>Now</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {NOTICES.map((n) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{n.date}</td>
            <td>{n.what.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + n.what.slice(1)}, by {n.by}</td>
            <td>{n.reason}{n.counter_notice ? " (a counter-notice was filed)" : ""}</td>
            <td class="text">{n.notice || "—"}</td>
            <td>{n.state === "restored" ? <span class="ok">restored {n.updated}</span> : <span class="warning">hidden</span>}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  )}
</Base>
